# proto-file: humanoid_nmpc/humanoid_mpc_msgs/dodgeball_throw.proto
# proto-message: humanoid_mpc_msgs.DodgeballThrow
# A payload exactly as the GUI Dodgeball tab publishes it (remote_control/tk_app/dodgeball.py throw_payload for
# azimuth 30 deg, elevation 15 deg, 3 m, 9 m/s, 1.2 kg), dumped the way the tab dumps it. Shared by the C++ parser test and
# the Python payload test, so a key renamed on either side of the wire fails a test on that side.
